    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it doesn't feel human though. it feels like a math problem. i look at the numbers and the time i spent and there's just no way to break even. everything i do now just feels like i'm throwing more good money/time after bad. like i'm just trying to patch up a sinking ship when the whole ocean is already gone. it's just... it's exhausting to keep trying to fix something that's fundamentally broken.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable that the feeling of financial and temporal loss translates into a cold, calculating sense of impossibility. When the foundation is gone, the problem shifts from fixing the structure to figuring out what to build next, which is a monumental task. Instead of trying to \"patch up\" the old structure, perhaps consider a radical shift in perspective—what is the absolute smallest, most manageable thing you could do today that would feel like a genuine step toward *you*?",
      "source": "target",
